What’s in the Box

Undaunted: Stalingrad comes in a big, heavy box with a big, heavy price tag. There are two colossal stacks of cardboard tiles that are used to build the city-scapes the 2-players will fight over during the course of the campaign. In fact, if you lay out all the tiles in rows and number order, it’ll make a rough map of the historical city. One set of tiles is for the starting situation of the map. The other is a set of replacements for those tiles if the originals get destroyed or fortified as part of the action.

